---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import '../styles/fileflex.css';
import '../styles/platform.css';
import '../styles/financial.css';
import '../styles/lawfirm.css';

const blogs = [
  {
    title: 'Cybersecurity for Law Firms: The Priority of Zero Trust Data Access Security',
    blurb: 'Cybersecurity and Zero Trust Data Access security is crucial for law firms to protect sensitive client data, mitigate insider threats, comply with…',
    img: '/images/lawfirm/iStock-825810126-web-e1727981340953-400x300.jpg',
    href: 'https://fileflex.com/blog/cybersecurity-for-law-firms-the-priority-of-zero-trust-data-access-security/',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Law Firm — FileFlex Enterprise Enables Remote Access and Zero Trust Security"
  description="A boutique estate law firm restores secure remote NAS access with FileFlex Enterprise Zero Trust Data Access — no VPN, no cloud migration, low total cost of ownership."
>

<Nav />

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="lf-hero" aria-labelledby="lf-hero-heading">
  <div class="lf-hero__inner">
    <p class="lf-hero__eyebrow">LAW FIRM</p>
    <h1 id="lf-hero-heading" class="lf-hero__title">
      FileFlex Enterprise Enables Remote Access and Zero Trust Security for a Boutique Estate Law Firm
    </h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     PULL QUOTE — blue strip
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="lf-quote" aria-label="Customer quote">
  <div class="lf-quote__inner">
    <p class="lf-quote__text">
      &ldquo;We needed something simple, secure, and affordable&mdash;and FileFlex checked every box.
      We&rsquo;re back to working the way we want, and it just works&rdquo;
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     BODY — 4 image-left + text-right rows
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="fin-body" class="fin-body" aria-label="Case study details">
  <div class="fin-body__inner">

    <!-- Customer Overview -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/lawfirm/ip-LF-Panel3-web-1024x1024.jpg" alt="Estate law firm — personalized client service" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Customer Overview</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          This client is a small Texas-based law firm specializing in estate planning, probate, trusts,
          and guardianship. Led by a board-certified attorney with over 25 years of experience, the firm
          is known for its personalized, compassionate approach to helping families navigate complex
          legal matters. Operating without dedicated IT staff, the firm values simplicity, affordability,
          and security in its technology. While not tech focused, they offer virtual consultations and
          prioritize clear communication and accessible service. As a lean operation, they require
          solutions that are easy to deploy, easy to use, and cost-effective.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="fin-sep" />

    <!-- Challenge -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/lawfirm/ip-LF-Panel2-web-e1734469679436-1024x577.jpg" alt="NAS device — remote access challenge" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Challenge</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          The firm stored all client case files on a local NAS device. However, the NAS manufacturer
          discontinued its remote access feature, leaving the attorneys unable to access critical files
          when working from home. This created significant frustration, disrupted productivity, and posed
          an operational risk in today&rsquo;s hybrid work environment. The firm needed a solution that
          would restore remote access, protect sensitive legal data, and align with their limited budget
          and technical resources.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="fin-sep" />

    <!-- Why FileFlex Enterprise -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/lawfirm/law-firm.jpg" alt="Law firm — lightweight secure remote access" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Why FileFlex Enterprise</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          The firm chose FileFlex Enterprise as a lightweight, secure platform that restored and enhanced
          remote access to their NAS without requiring a cloud migration or VPN. The decision was driven
          by several factors: the low cost of FileFlex, its ease of use, ease of installation, and its
          Zero Trust Data Access (ZTDA) architecture that protects sensitive legal documents without
          technical overhead.
        </p>
        <ul class="fin-list">
          <li>FileFlex <strong>restored secure remote access</strong> to the existing NAS infrastructure without requiring VPNs or a shift to the cloud.</li>
          <li>FileFlex Enterprise offered <strong>a cost-effective solution</strong> that fit the firm&rsquo;s budget, delivering enterprise-grade functionality at a small-firm price.</li>
          <li>Its user-friendly interface made it <strong>ideal for a non-technical team</strong>&mdash;attorneys required little to no training to get started.</li>
          <li>The <strong>simple installation</strong> allowed the firm to get up and running without the help of outside consultants or IT specialists.</li>
          <li>The platform&rsquo;s <strong>Zero Trust Data Access architecture</strong> delivered advanced security with audit logging, granular access control, and data protection that met the firm&rsquo;s need for compliance and peace of mind.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="fin-sep" />

    <!-- Results -->
    <div class="fin-block fin-row">
      <div class="fin-row__media">
        <img src="/images/lawfirm/Law-firm-results-1-894x1024.jpg" alt="Law firm results — secure remote work" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="fin-row__copy">
        <h2 class="fin-h2">Results</h2>
        <p class="fin-p">
          With FileFlex, attorneys now securely access and manage files from home, and they&rsquo;ve been
          able to reorganize case files for greater efficiency. Most importantly, the firm now operates
          with the confidence that client data is safeguarded using Zero Trust principles&mdash;without
          needing IT expertise or added infrastructure.
        </p>
        <ul class="fin-list">
          <li>Attorneys can now <strong>work remotely with full access</strong> to their files, improving flexibility and productivity.</li>
          <li><strong>File organization and remote file navigation</strong> have become easier and more intuitive, streamlining case work.</li>
          <li>The firm <strong>avoided costly IT upgrades</strong> or cloud migrations, preserving their infrastructure investment.</li>
          <li>The <strong>low total cost of ownership</strong> met their budget constraints while still elevating operations.</li>
          <li>With <strong>Zero Trust security</strong> in place, the firm has greater confidence in the protection of sensitive client data.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     RELATED BLOG
     ============================================================ -->
<section id="fin-blogs" class="fin-section fin-section--white" aria-labelledby="lf-blogs-heading">
  <div class="fin-section__inner">
    <h2 id="lf-blogs-heading" class="fin-h2 fin-h2--center">Check Out This Related Blog</h2>
    <div class="fin-blog-grid lf-blog-grid">
      {blogs.map((b) => (
        <a class="fin-blog" href={b.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <img class="fin-blog__img" src={b.img} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="400" height="300" />
          <div class="fin-blog__body">
            <h3 class="fin-blog__title">{b.title}</h3>
            <p class="fin-blog__blurb">{b.blurb}</p>
            <span class="fin-blog__more">Read more →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
